# SRG-APP-000295-WSR-000012  -  CAT II
# The web server must set an absolute session timeout value of eight hours
# or less.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000295-WSR-000012
group:           V-206414
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-002361
control_rev5:    AC-12

contribution:    Splunk bounds the life of a session from its own configuration:
                 server.conf sessionTimeout caps the splunkd session and web.conf
                 tools.sessions.timeout caps the Splunk Web session, so the eight-hour
                 ceiling the check text names is expressible without anything outside the
                 product.

governs:         server.conf - Core server settings, including the certificates and protocols used to
                 protect management and replication traffic.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           server.conf [general] sessionTimeout matches ^([1-8]h?|([1-9][0-9]?|[1-3][0-9]{2}|4[0-7][0-9]|480)m|([1-9][0-9]{0,3}|1[0-9]{4}|2[0-7][0-9]{3}|28[0-7][0-9]{2}|28800)s)$
check:           web.conf [settings] tools.sessions.timeout present
check:           web.conf [settings] tools.sessions.timeout max 15
check:           web.conf [settings] tools.sessions.timeout min 2
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          server.conf [general] sessionTimeout https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/server.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] tools.sessions.timeout https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/manage-users/configure-user-session-timeouts
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Where a reverse proxy, load balancer or SSO gateway fronts Splunk Web, its
                 own absolute session or cookie lifetime must also be bounded at eight
                 hours or less, and that is the gateway's configuration.
external:        A SAML or OIDC identity provider's own session lifetime governs how
                 quickly a re-authentication actually challenges the user, and the identity
                 provider holds it.
external:        The product STIG scopes SPLK-CL-000010 to the search head.

citation:        tools.sessions.restart_persist matches ^(0|false)$ is removed as
                 invention. The setting governs only whether the session cookie survives
                 the browser quitting, and the specification states persistence holds only
                 "assuming the 'tools.sessions.timeout' has not been reached"
                 (web.conf.spec:934-941), so it cannot extend a session past the timeout
                 and does not decide an absolute ceiling. It defaults to true, appears in
                 neither the SRG check text ("close sessions after eight hours or less")
                 nor the product STIG fix text (which sets tools.session.timeout alone), so
                 requiring false reports a finding against compliant systems over a setting
                 that is not the control. The sessionTimeout regex is kept: it is
                 directionally correct against sessionTimeout = <nonnegative
                 integer>[s|m|h|d] with default "1" (1 hour) (server.conf.spec:73-78),
                 admitting 1-8 bare or with h, 1-480m and 1-28800s, all of which are eight
                 hours or less, and rejecting every d-suffixed value, each of which exceeds
                 it. Where the key is absent the documented 1-hour default satisfies the
                 bound. tools.sessions.timeout keeps the product STIG's max of 15 and gains
                 the specification's own floor of 2 (web.conf.spec:929-930), which is the
                 same key the authority's fix text sets.
finding:         Splunk does not bound the absolute life of a session at eight hours or
                 less: server.conf [general] sessionTimeout is set beyond eight hours, or
                 web.conf [settings] tools.sessions.timeout is unset or 16 or more minutes.
